3. Create your first Freestyle project
Open Jenkins dashboard.
Click New Item.
Enter project name: MyFirstJob.
Select Freestyle project.
Click OK.
Go to Build Steps.
Select Execute shell (Linux).
Enter:
echo "Hello Jenkins"
echo "Welcome to DevOps Lab"
whoami
pwd
date

Click Save.
Click Build Now.
Open Build History → Build Number → Console Output.
Expected result
Hello Jenkins
Welcome to DevOps Lab
jenkins
/var/lib/jenkins/workspace/MyFirstJob
4. GitHub integration with Jenkins
Steps:
Create a repository on GitHub.
Add your source code and push it.
Open Jenkins.
Click New Item → Freestyle project.
Go to Source Code Management.
Select Git.
Enter your repository URL.
Add credentials if the repository is private.
Specify branch: */main.
Under Build Steps, select Execute shell.
Example:
echo "Code downloaded from GitHub"
ls -la
11. Save → Build Now → Console Output.
For a public repository, credentials are generally not required.
5. Jenkins Pipeline project
Steps:
Click New Item.
Enter name: MyPipeline.
Select Pipeline.
Click OK.
Scroll down to Pipeline.
Select Pipeline script.
Paste this script:
pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {
        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                echo 'Building Application'
            }
        }

        stage('Test') {
            steps {
                echo 'Testing Application'
            }
        }

        stage('Deploy') {
            steps {
                echo 'Deploying Application'
            }
        }
    }
}

Click Save → Build Now.
Open Console Output or Stage View.
